# Supabase & Server Actions

## Client

- Single browser/server client: `src/lib/supabase.ts`
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
- Do not duplicate clients; extend `@/lib/supabase` if needed.

## Server Actions (`src/app/actions/`)

| Module | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `recipe.ts` | Recipe master, materials, routings |
| `inventory.ts` / `inventoryActions.ts` | Stock, ecount items |
| `ecount.ts` | Ecount API helpers |
| `notionActions.ts` | Notion calendar CRUD |
| `database.ts` | Generic DB utilities |

## Conventions

```ts
"use server";
// Return shape: { success: boolean, data?, error?, message? }
```

- Keep action responses consistent with existing `{ success, error }` pattern.
- Never commit `.env`, keys, or Notion tokens — use env vars or client localStorage for user-provided Notion keys only on dashboard.

## Tables (common)

`recipes`, `recipe_materials`, `process_routings`, `production_orders`, `ecount_items` — verify column names in existing queries before adding inserts.
